---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/img/selfie-peru.jpeg';
---

<Layout
  title="About · Jessica Loredo"
  description="Designer, painter, counseling intern, and game design graduate living in Kansas City."
>
  <section class="about">
    <header class="ab-head">
      <div class="ab-eyebrow">About</div>
      <h1 class="ab-title">I am many things and I am also just, Jesi</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="ab-grid">
      <div class="ab-portrait">
        <Image src={portrait} alt="Jessica Loredo" width={760} />
        <p class="ab-caption">Kansas City, Missouri</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-prose">
        <p>
          I've been making things on the internet since I was in high school, which is longer than I
          usually admit out loud. That turned into fifteen years of product design, most of it in
          K-12, and somewhere in the middle of it a master's in game design from SMU Guildhall.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm now most of the way through a master's in counseling. People tend to read that as a
          swerve. It has never felt like one. I spent years building things meant to help kids learn
          and kept arriving at questions product design doesn't answer on its own, so I went and
          studied the field that does.
        </p>

        <h2>How my brain works</h2>
        <p>
          I'm autistic and ADHD. In practice that means I read systems quickly and I'm pulled toward
          the parts everyone else routes around. When something is vague, I go in and stay there
          until it has a shape.
        </p>
        <p>
          It also means I work in a rhythm rather than at a constant rate. Some days go deep, some
          stay light, and the deep ones are where the real work happens. I've stopped apologising
          for that, partly because it's how I'm built and partly because I think it's right. We have
          tools that make us faster than we have ever been, which makes it more important, not less,
          to spend real time making sure we're building the right thing.
        </p>
        <p class="ab-pull">Speed is not the same as direction.</p>

        <h2>The rest of it</h2>
        <p>
          I paint and illustrate. Oils, watercolour, gouache, digital, collage, whatever the piece
          seems to want. I write. I build small products on nights and weekends because making
          something is the fastest way for me to understand it, and because it's fun, which is a
          sufficient reason on its own.
        </p>
        <p>
          I used to keep all of that in a separate box from the professional work. I don't anymore.
          The game design degree is why I understand motivation. The painting is why I think about
          composition before colour, in pictures and in products. The counseling training is why I
          believe a person's state when they arrive matters more than anything I put on a screen.
          None of it was a detour.
        </p>
        <p>
          I live in Kansas City. I'm working toward a trauma-informed private practice, and I keep
          the art and the more personal writing at
          <a href="https://heartandhues.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">heartandhues.com</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="ab-contact">
          <a href="mailto:jessica@jessicaloredo.com">jessica@jessicaloredo.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 150px 48px 96px;
  }

  .ab-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
  }

  .ab-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .ab-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.8vw, 58px);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .ab-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 320px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 72px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .ab-portrait {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    position: sticky;
    top: 108px;
  }

  .ab-portrait :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .ab-caption {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .ab-prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 22px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .ab-prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .ab-prose p {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .ab-prose a {
    color: var(--teal);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--teal);
  }

  .ab-pull {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.8vw, 30px) !important;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ink) !important;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--teal);
    padding-left: 22px;
    margin: 6px 0;
  }

  .ab-contact {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about { padding: 116px 24px 72px; }
    .ab-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .ab-portrait { position: static; max-width: 300px; }
    .ab-head { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  }
</style>
